# This Dockerfile has no COPY/ADD — it only installs apt packages and cargo
# tools — so it needs no build context at all. Sending one costs real time:
# ci.yml, fuzz.yml, release.yml and `docker compose build dev` all build it with
# context `.`, which on a working tree carrying data/ and target/ can mean tens
# of gigabytes uploaded to the daemon for nothing.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the context's root
# .dockerignore, so this applies to THIS Dockerfile only and leaves the other
# builds that legitimately need a full context (scripts/Dockerfile.gltf,
# scripts/Dockerfile.blender, …) alone.
**
